# UI rules (48h hackathon)

Use when editing pages, components, or styles. Pair with the **shadcn** Cursor plugin if the project uses shadcn/ui.

## Default stack
- Tailwind for layout and spacing.
- Prefer **shadcn/ui** primitives (`Button`, `Input`, `Card`, `Label`, `Textarea`) when already installed or when the user asks to set them up.
- Do not add a second UI kit (MUI, Chakra, Ant, Daisy) unless the user explicitly asks.
- Prefer **JavaScript** + existing project patterns.

## Look (anti-slop)
- One clear visual direction. Define CSS variables or Tailwind theme tokens once.
- Avoid: purple-on-white / purple-indigo gradients, glow everywhere, pill spam, multi-layer shadows, emoji decoration, generic “AI SaaS” card grids.
- Prefer: big readable type, one accent colour, strong contrast, generous whitespace, real hierarchy (title → action → result).
- First viewport: one job. Title, short line, primary CTA, result area. No dashboard clutter.

## Demo UX (non-negotiable)
- Every async action needs **loading**, **empty**, and **error** UI (or mock success).
- Buttons need clear labels (`Analyze`, `Submit`, not icon-only).
- Works on laptop and phone width (~375px). Tap targets large enough for a finger.
- Show the result **on the same path** the judges click. Do not hide success behind a buried menu.

## Motion
- Optional: 1–2 subtle fades/staggers (result appear). Skip fancy motion if it risks the build.
- Do not add Framer Motion unless asked or already in `package.json`.

## Process
- If shadcn is not initialized and the user wants nicer UI, run the official init / add components rather than hand-rolling Button CSS.
- Reuse `components/ui/*`. Do not duplicate primitives.
- Smallest diff. No redesign of unrelated pages.
